tive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible on macOS in:\n- v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n- v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]\n- v4.5.2.rc1.official [f782f6ad0]\n- v4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n- current latest custom build [98782b6c8]\n\nTested with macOS 26.2.0 and 11.7.10.\n\nNot reproducible on Windows.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.2.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M4 Pro (14 threads) - 48.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running the editor on macOS, if from a file browser you choose 'Show in File Manager' on an executable .app file, the selected application is launched instead of the containing folder being opened.\n\nThis also applies to the `OS.shell_show_in_file_manager()` function, even in exported projects.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a file browser from the editor.\n  This can be any file browser, including clicking the Import button from the project selector, choosing the save path for an export configuration, or even the editor's FileSystem dock if an .app file is copied into to the project.\n2. Change the file filter to `All Files (*.*)` and navigate to an .app file.\n3. Right-click the .app file and select `Show in File Manager`.\n\nExpected results: The folder containing the selected app is opened.\nActual results: The selected app is launched.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A\n\n<img width=\"1149\" height=\"828\" alt=\"A screenshot of a godot file picker.  A file called 'test.app' is selected and the context menu option 'Show in File Manager' is highlighted.\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3bf4376d-00ec-4c70-95ac-f93f23b5b6eb\" />","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3M